#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gcc-hub: one front door to the owner's own tools (Claude, gcc, models, machine).

`gcc <verb> [args]` runs the tool behind that verb with your arguments. With no
verb it lists them. `gcc agents` is built in: every startup entry (LaunchAgents
and the timed jobs gcc-cron runs) with a title, note, cadence, state and source,
and on/off switches.

Meant to be called through a zsh function named `gcc` that sends anything that
is not a hub verb to the real C compiler, so builds are never affected, and
falls back to the compiler if the hub is ever missing:
    gcc() { if command -v gcc-hub >/dev/null 2>&1; then gcc-hub --as-gcc "$@"; else command gcc "$@"; fi; }

Every data command takes --json; colour is off when piped, under NO_COLOR, or
TERM=dumb. Exit 0 ok, 1 failed, 2 usage. Plan:
~/.claude/assets/reports/20261010-gcc-fix-list/gcc-hub-plan.md
"""
